{ Hey guys. Welcome to my Fried Liver study! This is a monster of an attack with a very high win rate for white, and if you know the moves, it's completely crushing!

The fried liver starts off with the Italian Game, one of the oldest openings. It starts out: 1. e4 e5, 2. Nf3 Nc6, 3. Bc4. Try it out! }
1. e4 { [%csl Gf5,Gd5][%cal Ge4d5,Ge4f5] } 1... e5 { [%csl Rf4,Rd4][%cal Re5d4,Re5f4] } 2. Nf3 { [%csl Re5,Gd4][%cal Gf3e5,Gf3d4] } 2... Nc6 { [%csl Re5][%cal Rc6e5,Rc6d4] } 3. Bc4 { Great! You've now set up the Italian Game! Our bishop we just brought out targets black's weak f7 pawn.
Black has many options. According to the lichess database, the 2 most common moves, both tied at 33% for a total of 66%, are Bc5 and Nf6. } { [%csl Rf7][%cal Gc4f7] } *

