[Annotator "https://lichess.org/@/thereal_stockfish"]
[FEN "r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/2B1P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 4 4"]
[SetUp "1"]
[UTCDate "2024.07.07"]
[UTCTime "00:27:08"]
[Orientation "white"]
[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

4... Nf6 $32 { The other most common move is Nf6, attacking our e4 pawn and looking at some valuable squares.
Let's continue with the Fried Liver attack and play Ng5. } { [%cal Rf6e4,Rf6d5,Gf3g5] } 5. Ng5 $40 { Great! Our knight is in a very dangerous place for black. We can't play this if not for Nf6, because now Black's knight is blocking the queen from seeing the g5 square.
We now defend our pawn on e4 while also threatening a very nasty fork on f7, winning material! } { [%csl Rf6,Gd8,Gh8][%cal Rd8f6,Rg8f6,Gg5f7,Gg5e4] } 5... d5 $132 { Because of the forking threat, d5 is almost always played, with a 75% play rate. This makes sense, but also falls right into our trap. Play exd4 now, taking the pawn. } { [%csl Rd5][%cal Gc4d5,Ge4d5] } 6. exd5 { Great! We have a pawn now! Not wanting to lose material, Black almost always plays Nxd5. } { [%cal Rf6d5] } (6. Bb5 { This move does make sense, pinning the knight, but it unfortunately hangs a pawn and that's not good. } { [%csl Ge4][%cal Gb5e8,Rd5e4,Rf6e4,Gg5e4] }) 6... Nxd5 { Now you would probably think black is better, but in reality, not quite! According to the lichess database, White in this position has a 62% win rate! Can you find the winning move? } 7. Nxf7!! { And the winning move here is Nxf7, sacrificing the knight!
Kxf7 is almost universally played here, but that just lures the king out into the open where it can be hunted down.
Stockfish already gives this a +1.0 for White, aka: we're winning! } { [%cal Re8f7,Gf7h8,Gf7d8] } 7... Kxf7 { The king has taken our knight, but it doesn't matter. Stockfish still gives us +0.9 because Black's king is wide open, it's lost castling rights, and we can attack it relentlessly.
Let's continue with Qf3+, forking Black's king and knight. } { [%csl Rf7,Rd5][%cal Gd1f3,Re8f7,Gf3d5,Gf3f7] } 8. Qf3+! { Great move! We have now successfully done the Fried Liver attack 🔥
We have lots of pressure on the knight, and it looks like black's going to lose it soon.
This position already has a 69% win rate for White and it's ~+0.5 according to Stockfish.
Next chapters we'll look at some options for black and some interesting counterplay. } { [%csl Rf7,Rd5][%cal Gf3f7,Gf3d5,Gc4d5] } *

