[UTCTime "00:57:21"]
[Orientation "white"]
[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

1... Bc5!? { If Black knows about the Fried Liver attack, they may play Bc5. This is known as the Traxler Gambit.
If this happens, we should abort the mission. Just take a free pawn with Bxf7. To show why you shouldn't take with the knight, setting up that nice fork, let's play it! } { [%csl Rf7,Gf2][%cal Gc4f7,Rf8c5,Rc5f2] } 2. Nxf7?? { Well, that's not good. You have a nice fork, but now black will play Bxf2+. } { [%csl Gh8,Gd8,Gf2][%cal Gf7d8,Gf7h8,Rc5f2,Rf6e4] } 2... Bxf2+!! { Now your king is under attack!
This just seems like a stupid sacrifice, but according to Stockfish, all your advantage is gone. Your other pieces aren't developed and the ones that are are on stupid squares. Also, you won't be able to castle anymore.
Take the bishop. } { [%csl Ge1][%cal Rf2e1] } 3. Kxf2 { Now you're in trouble. The knight is going to take your pawn with check, and then the queen will come in. Black has a 64% win rate right now. In fact if you play it wrong it could get you checkmated!
Stockfish says it's equal, but to most humans it's losing. } { [%csl Ge4,Gf2][%cal Rf6e4,Rd8h4,Rh4f2,Re4f2] } *

