[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

{ Because of the Black's threat from last chapter, you'll want to keep your advantage by taking a free pawn with Bxf7+.

The king will need to move, losing castling rights, and you're just up a pawn. Black can't sacrifice their bishop anymore because they need to deal with the check. Our knight is also guarding the e4 pawn, so that's not a worry.

Stockfish says that this is +1.0 for White if White takes the pawn. } { [%csl Rf7][%cal Gc4f7,Gf7e8,Gg5e4,Rf6e4] }
2. Bxf7+! { As you can see, black will need to move out of the way with the king, losing castling rights. We can then get out of there with the bishop and since our knight protects e4, the Traxler Gambit isn't an issue here. } { [%cal Re8e7,Gf7e8,Re8f8,Gg5f7,Gg5e4] } 2... Ke7 *

[Event "The Fried Liver Attack!: Italian Game: Knight Attack - Black plays the Polerio Defense"]
[Date "2024.07.07"]
[Result "*"]
