9... Nb4! { This move is the better of the two for black. Now Black also has 3 pieces pointing at the Knight, so it would be foolish to take it.
The best move here is, according to Stockfish, Bb3, for some reason. You can do that, but I prefer to castle, and it's also the most common move, with a 53% win rate for white. } { [%csl Rd5][%cal Rb4d5,Re6d5,Rd8d5,Gc3d5,Gc4d5,Gf3d5] } 10. O-O { Great. Our king is safe while Black's king... isn't. We have a lot of pressure on the knight and we can kick one of the defenders on the next move with a3. Because of this, black will usually play c6.
Stockfish evaluates this as +0.7. We have a lot of pieces out, and even though Black is up 2 points, they have horrible king safety and poor development. } { [%cal Ga2a3,Rc7c6] } *

