9... Nd4?? { Ah, an excellent move by Black, the second most common. It attacks our queen with tempo! Too bad it's a blunder, as we can just take the knight with our bishop It also comes with check and is defended twice. } { [%cal Rd4f3,Gc4d5] } 10. Bxd5+ { Now Black's in a pickle. After the king moves the queen can just move out of the way with the knight. White's up a pawn and will probably castle soon.
It's not looking good for black right now with White's 65% win rate. As a bonus, 23% of the time, Black plays Ke7, blundering checkmate in 2 after Qf7+ Kd6, Ne4#!
According to Stockfish, the evaluation is +1.4. However, black could mess up at any time, leading to a quick ending. } *

